  "semantics_and_limits": [
    "C++ get_type_descriptor and DynamicType return const references to class-held handles; corresponding Rust methods return borrowed static RuntimeType descriptors without adding a caller reference.",
    "RuntimeTyped::static_type_handle and Transient::dynamic_type_handle explicitly copy those descriptors into owning Rust Handles; the native probe and Rust tests confirm the 1 -> 2 -> 1 reference-count sequence.",
    "Rust does not expose the borrowed C++ Handle wrapper type; raw registry entries remain leaked, so explicit Register/destructor lifetime parity remains partial as recorded in runtime-type-owning-descriptors.json.",
    "The six rows are exact compiler IDs and unique Rust paths; this does not infer method coverage from a DEFINE_STANDARD_RTTIEXT macro name alone."
